.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rayscan-scan 1  "scan " 
.SH NAME
rayscan\-scan \- Scan TCP ports on one or more targets
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBscan\fR [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-target\fR] [\fB\-\-target\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-exclude\fR] [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-ports\fR] [\fB\-\-top\-ports\fR] [\fB\-\-preset\fR] [\fB\-\-exclude\-ports\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-profile\fR] [\fB\-\-stealth\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-\-probe\-timeout\-ms\fR] [\fB\-\-connect\-timeout\-ms\fR] [\fB\-\-rate\fR] [\fB\-\-workers\fR] [\fB\-\-retries\fR] [\fB\-\-randomize\fR] [\fB\-\-sequential\fR] [\fB\-\-jitter\-ms\fR] [\fB\-\-decoys\fR] [\fB\-\-fragment\-size\fR] [\fB\-\-ttl\fR] [\fB\-\-source\-port\-range\fR] [\fB\-\-top\-ports\-first\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-top\-ports\-first\fR] [\fB\-\-discover\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-live\fR] [\fB\-\-connect\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-verify\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-service\-detection\fR] [\fB\-\-udp\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-udp\-probe\fR] [\fB\-\-tls\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-tls\fR] [\fB\-\-os\fR] [\fB\-\-os\-probes\fR] [\fB\-\-all\-states\fR] [\fB\-\-show\fR] [\fB\-4\fR|\fB\-\-ipv4\fR] [\fB\-6\fR|\fB\-\-ipv6\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-syn\fR] [\fB\-\-ack\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-aimd\fR] [\fB\-\-rate\-auto\fR] [\fB\-\-host\-concurrency\fR] [\fB\-\-aimd\-min\-rate\fR] [\fB\-\-retry\-rate\fR] [\fB\-\-anomaly\-threshold\fR] [\fB\-\-resume\fR] [\fB\-\-save\-state\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-confidence\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-\-defense\fR] [\fB\-\-advisories\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-db\-update\fR] [\fB\-\-diff\fR] [\fB\-\-save\-baseline\fR] [\fB\-\-alert\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-fail\-on\-change\fR] [\fB\-\-ping\-sweep\fR] [\fB\-\-ping\-count\fR] [\fB\-\-ping\-timeout\-ms\fR] [\fB\-\-ndp\fR] [\fB\-\-ndp\-timeout\-ms\fR] [\fB\-\-plugins\fR] [\fB\-\-scripts\fR] [\fB\-\-scripts\-library\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-intrusive\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-severity\fR] [\fB\-\-scope\fR] [\fB\-\-force\-out\-of\-scope\fR] [\fB\-\-kev\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-epss\fR] [\fB\-\-stream\fR] [\fB\-\-shard\-index\fR] [\fB\-\-shard\-count\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scan TCP ports on one or more targets
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-target\fR \fI<TARGET>\fR
Target host, IP, CIDR, range, or file path. Repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-file\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Read targets from a file, one target or CIDR per line. Repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-exclude\fR \fI<TARGET>\fR
Exclude a target, CIDR, range, or @file. Repeatable
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-ports\fR \fI<PORTS>\fR
Ports to scan, for example 80,443,8000\-8100. Defaults to 1\-1024 if omitted
.TP
\fB\-\-top\-ports\fR \fI<N>\fR
Scan the top N most common ports (e.g. 10, 100, 1000)
.TP
\fB\-\-preset\fR \fI<PRESET>\fR
Port preset bundle (e.g. dc, win, web, linux, ot, full, q)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
dc: Active Directory / Domain Controller core services
.IP \(bu 2
win: Windows workstation/server typical services
.IP \(bu 2
web: HTTP(S) admin and alternate web ports
.IP \(bu 2
linux: Common Linux daemons (SSH, SMTP, DNS, NFS, DBs, etc.)
.IP \(bu 2
ot: Industrial control and SCADA control\-plane services
.IP \(bu 2
full: Full TCP range 1\-65535
.IP \(bu 2
q: nmap top\-1000 most frequent TCP ports
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-exclude\-ports\fR \fI<PORTS>\fR
Exclude ports from the scan, for example 22,135,445 or 8000\-8100
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the benchmark\-compatible JSON report
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
Output format
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
table
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
jsonl
.IP \(bu 2
csv
.IP \(bu 2
nmap\-xml: Nmap\-compatible XML output (compatible with nmap parsers / Metasploit)
.IP \(bu 2
greppable: Greppable output — one line per host, Nmap \-oG style
.IP \(bu 2
sarif: SARIF 2.1.0 report for code\-scanning and vulnerability dashboards
.IP \(bu 2
markdown: Human\-readable Markdown report for tickets and pull requests
.IP \(bu 2
host\-port: Plain `host:port` list — one open port per line for pipeline chaining
.IP \(bu 2
port\-list: Comma\-separated port numbers only — ready to paste into \-p of any tool. Without \-\-ports/\-\-top\-ports this discovery format scans the full TCP range (1\-65535). Example: 53,88,139,445,3389,5985
.RE
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write results to a file instead of stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI<PROFILE>\fR
Configuration profile
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
fast
.IP \(bu 2
balanced
.IP \(bu 2
careful
.IP \(bu 2
stealth
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-stealth\fR
Enable stealth mode (slow rate 20 pps, randomized order, high retries)
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Read settings from a TOML file. Defaults to rayscan.toml if present
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<SECONDS>\fR
Per\-connect timeout ceiling in seconds
.TP
\fB\-\-probe\-timeout\-ms\fR \fI<MS>\fR
How long to wait for a banner before calling a handshake silent, in ms
.TP
\fB\-\-connect\-timeout\-ms\fR \fI<MS>\fR
Per\-connect timeout ceiling in milliseconds. Overrides \-\-timeout
.TP
\fB\-\-rate\fR \fI<N>\fR
Global probes per second. 0 means unlimited
.TP
\fB\-\-workers\fR \fI<N>\fR
Worker count. 0 means automatic: cores × 32 capped at 512, bounded by RLIMIT_NOFILE
.TP
\fB\-\-retries\fR \fI<N>\fR
Retries for local resource failures such as EMFILE
.TP
\fB\-\-randomize\fR
Shuffle target and port order
.TP
\fB\-\-sequential\fR
Keep target and port order. Overrides config randomize
.TP
\fB\-\-jitter\-ms\fR \fI<MS>\fR
Maximum random delay before each probe, in milliseconds (0\-5000)
.TP
\fB\-\-decoys\fR \fI<IP,IP>\fR
Spoofed source addresses for decoy probes, comma\-separated (max 8). Requires \-\-syn
.TP
\fB\-\-fragment\-size\fR \fI<BYTES>\fR
Fragment raw SYN probes into IP fragments of this payload size (multiple of 8, 8\-1480). Requires \-\-syn
.TP
\fB\-\-ttl\fR \fI<N>\fR
IP TTL / IPv6 hop limit for raw SYN, ACK, and OS fingerprint probes (1\-255). Requires \-\-syn, \-\-ack, or \-\-os
.TP
\fB\-\-source\-port\-range\fR \fI<MIN\-MAX>\fR
Source port range for raw SYN/ACK probes, as MIN\-MAX (1\-65535). Requires \-\-syn or \-\-ack
.TP
\fB\-\-top\-ports\-first\fR
Scan most common ports first to minimize time\-to\-first\-result
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-top\-ports\-first\fR
Disable top ports prioritization (keep sequential or natural order)
.TP
\fB\-\-discover\-only\fR
Fast discovery mode: report open ports immediately without service/banner inspection
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-live\fR
Disable real\-time live results table streaming during scan
.TP
\fB\-\-connect\-only\fR
Report handshake success as open without banner or connect verification
.TP
\fB\-\-verify\fR
Verify that a handshake yields a banner or immediate close
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-service\-detection\fR
Disable banner\-based service and version detection
.TP
\fB\-\-udp\fR
Enable UDP service detection (passive banner read + optional active probe)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-udp\-probe\fR
Disable UDP active probe; only perform the initial passive banner read
.TP
\fB\-\-tls\fR
Inspect TLS on every open TCP port (certificate, version, cipher)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-tls\fR
Disable automatic TLS inspection of known TLS/STARTTLS ports
.TP
\fB\-\-os\fR
Enable OS fingerprinting via TCP/IP stack analysis (requires root/CAP_NET_RAW). Probes up to \-\-os\-probes open ports per host and classifies the SYN\-ACK replies
.TP
\fB\-\-os\-probes\fR \fI<N>\fR
Open\-port samples per host for the OS fingerprint consensus (1\-8, default: 3)
.TP
\fB\-\-all\-states\fR
Show every port state
.TP
\fB\-\-show\fR \fI<STATE>\fR
States to display. Repeat or comma\-separate
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
open
.IP \(bu 2
closed
.IP \(bu 2
filtered
.IP \(bu 2
unfiltered
.IP \(bu 2
silent
.IP \(bu 2
unreachable
.IP \(bu 2
error
.IP \(bu 2
all
.RE
.TP
\fB\-4\fR, \fB\-\-ipv4\fR
Resolve and scan only IPv4 targets
.TP
\fB\-6\fR, \fB\-\-ipv6\fR
Resolve and scan only IPv6 targets
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress progress and status messages
.TP
\fB\-\-syn\fR
Use raw SYN discovery, then verify responsive ports (root/CAP_NET_RAW, Linux only)
.TP
\fB\-\-ack\fR
TCP ACK scan to map firewall filtering (root/CAP_NET_RAW, Linux only). Unfiltered ports answer with RST; filtered ports stay silent
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-aimd\fR
Disable AIMD adaptive rate control during raw SYN scanning
.TP
\fB\-\-rate\-auto\fR
Enable adaptive rate control for connect scans (detect rate limiting and back off)
.TP
\fB\-\-host\-concurrency\fR \fI<N>\fR
Maximum concurrent connect attempts per target host (0 = unlimited)
.TP
\fB\-\-aimd\-min\-rate\fR \fI<N>\fR
AIMD minimum rate floor in packets per second (default: 100)
.TP
\fB\-\-retry\-rate\fR \fI<N>\fR
Rate used for SYN retransmission passes in packets per second. 0 means auto (rate / 4, minimum 100). Default: 0
.TP
\fB\-\-anomaly\-threshold\fR \fI<N>\fR
Per\-host SYN\-open count above which the host is treated as anomalous (tarpit/SYN\-proxy farm) and verification is sampled.  0 disables. Default: 1000
.TP
\fB\-\-resume\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Resume a previous interrupted scan from a saved state file. Ports already probed in the state file are skipped; results are merged
.TP
\fB\-\-save\-state\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Save scan state to a file on completion or interruption (Ctrl\-C). Use with \-\-resume to continue an interrupted scan
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-confidence\fR \fI<PERCENT>\fR
Filter results to only show ports with confidence score >= N percent (0\-100)
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR [\fI<PORT>\fR]
Print comprehensive evidence and accuracy breakdown for all ports or a specific port
.TP
\fB\-\-defense\fR
Always display detailed defense and middlebox intelligence assessment
.TP
\fB\-\-advisories\fR
Correlate detected service versions against the local and bundled CVE advisory databases
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-db\-update\fR
Skip the automatic NVD advisory database refresh check before scanning
.TP
\fB\-\-diff\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Compare scan results against a previous scan JSON report or state file to detect changes
.TP
\fB\-\-save\-baseline\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Save the final report as a JSON baseline for future \-\-diff comparisons
.TP
\fB\-\-alert\-file\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write a concise change alert to FILE (requires \-\-diff; written on every run)
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-on\-change\fR
Exit with status 1 when \-\-diff detects any new, gone, or modified port
.TP
\fB\-\-ping\-sweep\fR
Discover responsive hosts with ICMP echo/TCP ping before scanning
.TP
\fB\-\-ping\-count\fR \fI<N>\fR
Ping probes per host (1\-10). Requires \-\-ping\-sweep
.TP
\fB\-\-ping\-timeout\-ms\fR \fI<MS>\fR
Per\-ping timeout in milliseconds (50\-10000). Requires \-\-ping\-sweep
.TP
\fB\-\-ndp\fR
Discover local IPv6 neighbors with an NDP all\-nodes multicast probe. Expands broad IPv6 CIDRs such as /64 instead of enumerating every address
.TP
\fB\-\-ndp\-timeout\-ms\fR \fI<MS>\fR
NDP discovery timeout in milliseconds (50\-5000). Requires \-\-ndp
.TP
\fB\-\-plugins\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Directory or TOML file with declarative probe packs
.TP
\fB\-\-scripts\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
TOML manifest or directory of script plugin manifests (sidecar or WASM). Repeatable; every path contributes packs to the same registry
.TP
\fB\-\-scripts\-library\fR
Load script packs installed in the local library (see `rayscan scripts`)
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-intrusive\fR
Allow script plugins whose manifest sets danger = "intrusive"
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-severity\fR \fI<SEVERITY>\fR
Drop script findings below this severity (info < low < medium < high < critical)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
info
.IP \(bu 2
low
.IP \(bu 2
medium
.IP \(bu 2
high
.IP \(bu 2
critical
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-scope\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Scope definition file (TOML or plaintext) specifying authorized target boundaries
.TP
\fB\-\-force\-out\-of\-scope\fR
Force scan execution even if targets violate the Scope Guard definition
.TP
\fB\-\-kev\-only\fR
Filter advisory findings to only display services with CISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-epss\fR \fI<SCORE>\fR
Filter advisory findings to those with EPSS exploitation probability >= SCORE (0.0\-1.0)
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Stream JSONL port findings immediately to stdout as each candidate is verified
.TP
\fB\-\-shard\-index\fR \fI<N>\fR
Scan only this shard of the target list (0\-based). Requires \-\-shard\-count
.TP
\fB\-\-shard\-count\fR \fI<N>\fR
Split targets into N deterministic shards for distributed scans. Requires \-\-shard\-index
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
